ED_DecisionText:
A 

At its 64th plenary meeting, on 15 December 2025, the General Assembly, on the recommendation of the Second Committee  (Footnote: A/80/555, para. 8, Draft decision 2.), recalling its resolution 79/327 of 5 September 2025, in particular the provisions relating to working methods, as well as its previous decisions on the revitalization of the work of the Second Committee, and recognizing the need for an approach that was complementary to other processes taking place during the eightieth session, including the work of the informal ad hoc working group on mandate implementation review, the Working Group on the Strengthening and Revitalizing of the Work of the General Assembly and the review of resolutions 75/290 A and B of 25 June 2021 on the strengthening of the Economic and Social Council and the format and organizational aspects of the high-level political forum on sustainable development:

(a)	Decided that the Bureau of the Second Committee would organize a series of informal dialogues and consultations to discuss the revitalization of the work of the Committee, with the first such dialogue to be held in February 2026, preceded by informal engagement by the Bureau with Member States to raise awareness of the process, and requested the Bureau to finalize and circulate a road map following the first dialogue, including a timeline, proposed focus areas and modalities of further discussion;

(b)	Also decided that the Second Committee would convene a plenary meeting following those dialogues to take stock of the deliberations and, as appropriate, take action on any recommendations, for subsequent approval by the General Assembly, to allow any change to come into effect ahead of the eighty-first session.

B 

[80/520 B. Revitalization of the work of the Second Committee
B [Footnote: Decision 80/520, in section B.5 of the Official Records of the General Assembly, Eightieth Session, Supplement No. 49 (A/80/49), vol. II, becomes decision 80/520 A.]
At its 107th plenary meeting, on 28 July 2026, the General Assembly, on the recommendation of the Second Committee,  (Footnote: A/80/555/Add.1, para4.): 
(a) Reaffirmed its resolution 79/327 of 5 September 2025 and all previous resolutions relating to the revitalization of the work of the General Assembly, as well as its decisions 74/537 B of 11 August 2020, 75/548 B of 29 July 2021 and 80/520 of 15 December 2025 and other relevant decisions on the revitalization of the work of the Second Committee, and the need for their full implementation;
(b) Recognized the importance of other reform, revitalization and rationalization processes under way across the United Nations system with a focus on development;
(c) Requested the Second Committee to take concrete steps to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of its working methods and complementarity across the system, and to take a consistent approach to applying the relevant UN80 mandate implementation review outcomes adopted by the General Assembly, in accordance with the Committee’s intergovernmental decision-making processes;
(d) Reaffirmed that the revitalization of the Second Committee aimed to strengthen the work of the Committee and to ensure that its core focus remained on the development pillar of the United Nations;
(e) Noted that the work of the Second Committee should support the implementation of the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development,1 while recognizing that the purview of the Committee is broader;
(f) Decided:
(i) To request the Bureau of the Committee at the eighty-first session, taking into account the proposals made during the revitalization discussion at the eightieth session, and in consultation with the wider membership and with the support of the Secretariat, to continue to make proposals to streamline the first phase of the Committee’s work with a view to improving interaction and efficiency, including through the joint consideration of one or more agenda items, the efficient use of available plenary time, the adjustment of submission deadlines and, where possible, the introduction of draft proposals during the consideration of the relevant agenda items;
(ii) To combine the annual joint meeting of the Committee and the Economic and Social Council and one Committee-organized side event into a single joint thematic meeting, to focus on a theme related to that of the Committee’s general debate, drawing on the comparative perspectives and expertise of the two bodies;
(iii) To hold the dialogue with the Executive Secretaries of the regional commissions in a manner and at a time that maximizes its relevance, contributions, engagement and participation and avoids overlap with the intensive phase of informal consultations;
(iv) To invite the Chair of the Committee to prepare and circulate informal summaries of the joint thematic meeting and the dialogue with the regional commissions;
(v) To request the preparation of more concise, analytical and forward-looking reports that directly support the work of the Second Committee, highlighting developments that have occurred since the adoption of the mandating resolutions, to call for the timely submission and issuance of mandated reports as much in advance of the consideration of the related agenda items as possible, in accordance with its resolution 80/234 of 30 December 2025, and to request the Secretariat to inform the Bureau in case of delays in issuance of mandated reports;
(g) In accordance with the rules of procedure of the General Assembly, without prejudice to the sovereign right of Member States to submit draft proposals, and while recognizing that there was no standard applicable approach, decided: (i) To reiterate the measures outlined in resolution 79/327 regarding the frequency, length and number of resolutions, international commemorations and resolutions with a regional scope;
(ii) To invite proponents to streamline draft resolutions, with a view to making them more concise, focused and action-oriented and enhancing their readability, including, as appropriate, by streamlining preambular language;
(iii) To invite delegations, where appropriate and on their own initiative, to engage informally at an early stage of the session, with a view to facilitating cross-regional engagement and improving mutual understanding;
(iv) To encourage restraint by delegations in submitting new draft resolutions to the Second Committee, taking into account the wider efforts of the Committee to optimize the consideration of its programme of work and to enhance the efficiency and predictability of its work;
(v) That the deadline for the submission of new draft proposals shall be the organizational meeting of the Committee;
(vi) To invite delegations, where appropriate, to take into account the outcomes of major United Nations conferences and high-level meetings with related substantive focus, with a view to promoting complementarity and avoiding overlap in the Committee’s substantive consideration;
(vii) To also invite delegations, as appropriate, to take into account, in the submission of draft proposals, the provisions of its resolution 77/335 of 1 September 2023, aimed at avoiding overlap and duplication in the agendas of its Main Committees;
(h) Encouraged the Bureau to continue, in line with existing practice, exercising its role in identifying, coordinating and providing ongoing guidance to facilitators and co-facilitators of draft proposals; to continue preparing, with the support of the Secretariat, a predictable and transparent schedule of informal consultations on draft resolutions; to provide as much time as possible between such consultations to allow groups and delegations to coordinate their positions; and to encourage facilitators and co-facilitators to consider limiting the number of rounds of consultation, as possible, particularly where substantive discussion is limited, and inform the Bureau accordingly, with a view to optimizing the calendar of consultations;
(i) Reiterated the importance of holding open, transparent, inclusive, text-based and line-by-line informal consultations on draft resolutions;
(j) Invited delegations to consider volunteering to take part in facilitation and co-facilitation of draft resolutions before the Committee, in line with existing practice;
(k) Requested the Bureau to continue enhancing the transparency of the working methods of the Second Committee, with a view to ensuring that all delegations remain informed of relevant procedures, rules and practices, throughout the negotiation process and adoption;
(l) Agreedto continue reviewing the frequency of agenda items and resolutions on a case-by-case basis, in consultation with Member States, with a view to rationalizing the workload of the Committee while preserving its ability to address priority development issues;
(m) Decided:
(i) To consider the item entitled “Information and communications technologies for sustainable development” and the resolution of the same title at its eighty-first session and every other year thereafter;
(ii) That the sub-item entitled “Commodities” would be discontinued as of the eighty-second session and that the subject matter of the resolution on commodities would be addressed within the resolution on international trade and development, starting from the eighty-second session, and requests the inclusion of a special section on the matter starting from the eighty-second session and thereafter in future reports of the Secretary-General on international trade and development, recognizing that the resolution might be brought back in the future if deemed necessary;
(iii) To consider the sub-item entitled “Promoting investments for sustainable development” and the resolution of the same title at the eighty-first session and every other year thereafter;
(iv) That the subject matter of the resolution on the pivotal role of reliable and stable energy connectivity in driving sustainable development would be addressed within the resolution on ensuring access to affordable, reliable, sustainable and modern energy for all, beginning from the eighty-first session, and requested the inclusion of a special section on the matter starting from the eighty-first session and thereafter in future reports of the Secretary-General on ensuring access to affordable, reliable, sustainable and modern energy for all, recognizing that the resolution may be brought back in the future if deemed necessary;
(v) To consider the resolution entitled “Towards the sustainable development of the Caribbean Sea for present and future generations” at its eighty-first session and every three years thereafter;
(vi) That the sub-item entitled “Implementation of the United Nations Convention to Combat Desertification in Those Countries Experiencing Serious Drought and/or Desertification, Particularly in Africa” and the resolution of the same title will next be included in the agenda of the eighty-second session, and be considered every other year thereafter;
(vii) That the sub-item entitled “Convention on Biological Diversity” and the resolution on the implementation of the Convention on Biological Diversity and its contribution to sustainable development would next be included in the agenda of the eighty-second session, and be considered every other year thereafter;
(viii) To consider the sub-item entitled “Harmony with Nature” and the resolution of the same title at its eighty-first session and every three years thereafter;
(ix) That the sub-item entitled “Human resources development” would be discontinued as of the eighty-first session and the subject matter of the resolution on human resources development would be addressed within the resolution on education for sustainable development in the framework of the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development, starting from the eighty-second session, and requested the inclusion of a special section on the matter starting from the eighty-second session and thereafter in future reports of the Secretary-General on education for sustainable development in the framework of the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development, recognizing that the resolution may be brought back in the future if deemed necessary;
(n) Also decided:
(i) To request the Bureau to update conference room paper A/C.2/79/CRP.2 on the working methods of the Second Committee, following each main session;
(ii) To request incoming Bureaux to meet with outgoing Bureaux by July each year in order to consult on and review issues relating to the efficient functioning of the Committee and to recommend, as appropriate, further improvements for the coming session;
(iii) To review and assess during the eighty-fifth session the implementation of the current decision and its impact on the efficiency and effectiveness of the work of the Committee.
